Subject: [Krypton] Require explicit Widevine consent before loading or updating

Helium allows CRLSet and Widevine components. Krypton's older fallback used
general services consent for the upstream component server. Require the new
default-off Widevine startup choice for its component registration and every
CDM publication path, including a previously downloaded copy. Enabling it also
authorizes upstream component requests without enabling other services.
CRLSet and the existing services-consent path remain unchanged. This is the
brief's intentional exception to the old default: existing installs must opt
in again for Widevine playback; all other off-state decisions remain Helium's.

